GENERATE_FUTURE_MAP_PROMPT = '\nYou are planning the narrative dependencies of a serialized short-form drama. Working backward from the actual ending in the complete episode outlines, build a Future Map, also called a Backward Narrative Dependency Tree: a tree of necessary future narrative goals.\n\n## Complete episode outlines\n{{EpisodeOutline}}\n\nDefinitions:\n- The root is the concrete ending actually achieved in the outlines, not a broad theme.\n- Each child answers: What narrative goal or condition must first be met for its parent to become credible?\n- Continue decomposing until the leaves are specific foundational setups, initial conditions, motivations, knowledge, or relationships.\n- This is an abstract tree of causal and narrative dependencies, not an episode index, timeline, or recap.\n\nConstraints:\n1. Use only plot, outcomes, characters, conflicts, and causal links established in the episode outlines. Do not invent events.\n2. Do not map one episode to one node or put episode numbers in nodes. Let the narrative goal determine granularity.\n3. Every non-root node has exactly one parent_id. A child goal supports its parent goal.\n4. The root is `FM001`, with parent_id null and depth 0. Other nodes have unique sequential IDs `FM002`, `FM003`, etc.; depth equals parent depth plus one.\n5. Sibling goals should be distinct and together explain the key conditions for their parent. Avoid synonyms, trivial actions, and vague goals.\n6. State each goal as a clear, verifiable completion condition. Explain in requirement why it is necessary for the parent; summarize specific supporting outline evidence without episode numbers.\n7. Output JSON only, without commentary.\n\nFormat:\n```json\n{\n  "map_type": "backward_requirement_tree",\n  "root_id": "FM001",\n  "nodes": [\n    {"node_id": "FM001", "parent_id": null, "depth": 0,\n     "goal": "Concrete final outcome", "requirement": "The series\' ultimate narrative result",\n     "evidence": "Supporting ending in the outlines"},\n    {"node_id": "FM002", "parent_id": "FM001", "depth": 1,\n     "goal": "Necessary subgoal supporting the ending",\n     "requirement": "Why the parent depends on this subgoal",\n     "evidence": "Supporting plot in the outlines"}\n  ]\n}\n```\n'
GENERATE_EPISODE_CONTRIBUTIONS_PROMPT = '\nYou are planning the narrative dependencies of a serialized short-form drama. Using only the complete episode outlines and the existing Future Map, determine which future narrative goals each episode actually advances.\n\n## Complete episode outlines\n{{EpisodeOutline}}\n\n## Future Map\n{{FutureMap}}\n\nA contribution means that specific events in an episode provide necessary setup, progress, a turning point, completion, or payoff for a node. Sharing a character, theme, or nearby point in time is not enough.\n\nConstraints:\n1. Output exactly one episode record for every episode in the outlines, ordered by episode_id.\n2. An episode may contribute to one or more nodes.\n3. node_id must refer to an existing Future Map node.\n4. contribution_type must be one of `setup` (establishes a prerequisite, motive, knowledge, or relationship), `advance` (material progress), `turn` (pivotal shift, escalation, or setback), `complete` (direct achievement), or `payoff` (realization of an accumulated dramatic effect).\n5. State concretely which episode event contributes and how.\n6. importance is `primary` or `secondary`. Mark only the episode\'s central contribution as primary.\n7. Do not associate the same node twice with one episode.\n8. Do not invent events absent from the outlines.\n9. Output JSON only, without commentary.\n\nFormat:\n```json\n{\n  "episodes": [\n    {"episode_id": 1, "contributions": [\n      {"node_id": "FM010", "contribution_type": "setup", "importance": "primary",\n       "contribution": "How this episode\'s specific events establish a prerequisite"}\n    ]}\n  ]\n}\n```\n'
